        {
          "id": 1442615542,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "\"Note: The APN field is not encoded as a dotted string as commonly used in documentation.\"\n\nMy reading is that means \"it's not a string with actual periods/full stops (as written in documentation), it's encoded with length values before each token as a DNS name.\"\n\nIn practice, I have seen both, and I think we have a few dissectors that examine the first byte, and if it's ASCII printable treat it as a string, and if it's less than 0x30 treat is as ENC_APN_STR.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
