        {
          "id": 1443417664,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Ah, I see, you're right, my apologies. It's more obvious to me when it's phrased in TS 29.244 8.2.38:\n\n> NOTE 1: The FQDN field in the IE is not encoded as a dotted string as commonly used in DNS master zone files\n\n\"As commonly used in DNS master zone files\" is unambiguous to me. \"As commonly used in documentation\" was confusing. Otherwise the phrasing is the same, so it's probably the same meaning.\n\nI am convinced it's a string.",
